01:45:19.486 --> 01:45:22.784
have received that. Okay.

01:45:22.912 --> 01:45:27.248
So I would like to at this point open

01:45:27.304 --> 01:45:30.896
the floor and call upon any members of the public who have not spoken,

01:45:31.008 --> 01:45:35.296
who wish to speak at today's public meeting to

01:45:35.368 --> 01:45:38.736
come to the podium. And if you do wish to speak, you will

01:45:38.808 --> 01:45:41.888
have three minutes. Please state your full name,

01:45:41.944 --> 01:45:45.872
municipality in which you reside for the record and

01:45:45.896 --> 01:45:49.114
then if there are questions after, please hold on a moment.

01:45:49.162 --> 01:45:53.390
So if there is anybody who has not spoken, do see one individual.

01:45:53.970 --> 01:45:57.434
Thank you. You have three minutes and your name in the municipality you

01:45:57.442 --> 01:45:58.150
were in.

01:46:03.010 --> 01:46:06.474
Turn the mic on Rick Chambers

01:46:06.522 --> 01:46:10.138
from the City of Waterloo. I'm on the Age Friendly

01:46:10.154 --> 01:46:13.670
Committee in the City of Waterloo, an age friendly network for the for the region.

01:46:14.310 --> 01:46:17.486
I'm looking at a sheet of paper that I presented here on

01:46:17.558 --> 01:46:20.942
December 8, 2021 and not much has

01:46:20.966 --> 01:46:24.734
changed. I just want to mention that at that time I asked for,

01:46:24.822 --> 01:46:28.078
or we asked for free rides for older adults

01:46:28.174 --> 01:46:31.758
over 65 during off peak hours and on certain days of the week.

01:46:31.894 --> 01:46:35.050
As Swanee was mentioning earlier,

01:46:35.430 --> 01:46:38.846
we were talking about the environmental reasons to do this and

01:46:38.918 --> 01:46:42.222
I think we've been through that tonight and then social reasons as

01:46:42.246 --> 01:46:45.614
well. I think this region is going to

01:46:45.622 --> 01:46:49.150
have 25 to 30% of their population over

01:46:49.270 --> 01:46:53.070
65 in five years. In the last eight to 10 years of their

01:46:53.110 --> 01:46:56.894
lives. They will not be able to drive. So knowing how to use public transit

01:46:56.942 --> 01:47:00.542
is very important and the GRT does a good job with

01:47:00.566 --> 01:47:04.810
the ride a Bus program and other things to help people learn that.

01:47:05.110 --> 01:47:09.204
However, there's, there's still the issue, as Brian Paul mentioned,

01:47:09.252 --> 01:47:12.260
about the cost of this and the frequency. And as

01:47:12.300 --> 01:47:15.844
Swanee pointed out as well, making it available to people

01:47:16.012 --> 01:47:20.132
on a free basis is the most positive

01:47:20.196 --> 01:47:23.492
way to look at this. Recent research shows that as a society,

01:47:23.556 --> 01:47:27.012
communities are ill prepared to provide adequate transit for the growing and

01:47:27.036 --> 01:47:30.244
increasing population of older adults. A McMaster University

01:47:30.332 --> 01:47:34.552
study in 2020 said that there is a broader ableist bias in transportation

01:47:34.616 --> 01:47:38.280
planning. Across Canada and elsewhere, transportation officials do not plan

01:47:38.320 --> 01:47:42.120
their services with enough attention to older adults.

01:47:42.280 --> 01:47:45.848
Free rides once per week or during off peak hours will enable older

01:47:45.864 --> 01:47:49.480
adults to learn how to use the system and fulfill the environmental and

01:47:49.520 --> 01:47:53.060
social reasons for using a public system.

01:47:53.440 --> 01:47:56.728
So again, we're still asking five years

01:47:56.784 --> 01:48:00.230
later. In fact, we started this about 10 years ago for

01:48:00.270 --> 01:48:03.910
free rides for older adults. I'm very pleased to see that free

01:48:03.950 --> 01:48:07.302
rides for children is happening. As and as Brian

01:48:07.366 --> 01:48:11.142
Paul pointed out, in other jurisdictions in this province and

01:48:11.246 --> 01:48:15.770
around the world, free rides for everyone is the rule.

01:48:16.110 --> 01:48:19.734
And if transit

01:48:19.782 --> 01:48:23.942
systems are not public services or social services and

01:48:23.966 --> 01:48:27.214
they're expected to run as a business, you're going to disenfranchise a

01:48:27.222 --> 01:48:30.302
lot of people who could be using the system to

01:48:30.326 --> 01:48:33.694
their advantage for all kinds of reasons. So I hope

01:48:33.702 --> 01:48:37.534
I don't have to do this again, but I wish you all the

01:48:37.542 --> 01:48:40.750
best in making these decisions. Thanks. Thank you, Rick.

01:48:40.830 --> 01:48:44.170
And I see no questions from council.

01:48:44.950 --> 01:48:46.610
Is there anybody else?

01:48:47.910 --> 01:48:50.782
Okay. I am not seeing any other individuals.

01:48:50.926 --> 01:48:54.484
Thank you all for coming. Oh, there is one. Okay. Yep. Your name and

01:48:54.492 --> 01:48:57.620
the municipality you're in. And you've got three minutes. First and last

01:48:57.660 --> 01:49:01.444
name? Yeah, Matthew Morgan and

01:49:01.452 --> 01:49:04.820
I'm from Waterloo and I have a few

01:49:04.860 --> 01:49:08.000
questions. One,

01:49:08.300 --> 01:49:11.560
what is the current timing for the construction of the transit hub?

01:49:12.300 --> 01:49:15.860
Two, when are we going to bring back trolley buses because

01:49:15.900 --> 01:49:19.160
they are more energy efficient, even better for the environment

01:49:19.620 --> 01:49:23.440
and don't need to be charged overnight, unlike battery buses.

01:49:23.860 --> 01:49:27.292
And three, so the CO people have mentioned already, what is

01:49:27.316 --> 01:49:31.000
the future of Ion stage two? And one more thing.

01:49:32.820 --> 01:49:34.920
What is Ion stage three about?

01:49:36.260 --> 01:49:40.252
Okay, Commissioner Spooner, I'm going to have you respond through

01:49:40.276 --> 01:49:44.124
your chair. Thank you for the question. So Kitchener central transit hub

01:49:44.172 --> 01:49:48.010
timeline planned to be operational in 2029 or

01:49:48.050 --> 01:49:51.354
2030, which I think is a good level of confidence

01:49:51.402 --> 01:49:55.194
at this time with a project of that complexity. Trolley buses,

01:49:55.242 --> 01:49:59.034
really interesting. We've had discussions about trolley buses as a propulsion

01:49:59.082 --> 01:50:02.298
technology. This council has supported us

01:50:02.354 --> 01:50:06.362
in exploring propulsion technologies from diesel to hybrid

01:50:06.426 --> 01:50:10.836
to electric and others. And so that absolutely fits in the other stage

01:50:10.868 --> 01:50:14.960
two. Ion, as I mentioned earlier, will come back to council in November for

01:50:15.740 --> 01:50:19.316
consideration of the option selection. An Ion

01:50:19.348 --> 01:50:23.556
stage three at this point is a corridor identified in the regional official plan

01:50:23.708 --> 01:50:27.236
that runs from Sunrise to the regional

01:50:27.268 --> 01:50:30.724
airport. So it's a planning piece at

01:50:30.732 --> 01:50:34.164
this point, but you know, obviously it suggests that we've got more rapid transit in

01:50:34.172 --> 01:50:36.890
our future. Thank you. Thank you.

01:50:38.950 --> 01:50:43.070
Okay. I would like to thank everyone for coming in

01:50:43.110 --> 01:50:46.622
and providing their input. Those who are virtual, those who've come in person and

01:50:46.646 --> 01:50:49.010
those who have submitted correspondence.

01:50:50.150 --> 01:50:53.454
All correspondence received by the regional Clerk's office regarding

01:50:53.502 --> 01:50:57.006
the GRT business plan have been compiled and included

01:50:57.038 --> 01:51:00.862
in the addendum for today's agenda for council's consideration

01:51:01.006 --> 01:51:04.648
and are received for information. Any correspondence that's

01:51:04.664 --> 01:51:07.880
been received after the addendum was released yesterday, I think,

01:51:07.920 --> 01:51:12.260
and there was the one that came in tonight and will be included in the.

01:51:13.520 --> 01:51:17.112
It will be sent to council, the next Sustainability, Infrastructure and

01:51:17.136 --> 01:51:20.312
Development Committee. We received correspondence from

01:51:20.336 --> 01:51:24.440
Luke Taylor, ryan Bean, Justin McLaughlin and Ellie

01:51:24.520 --> 01:51:27.898
Lu. And okay, so this concludes our meeting.

01:51:27.954 --> 01:51:31.370
The next meeting for sustainability, Infrastructure and development is

01:51:31.410 --> 01:51:34.986
May 6. And we will now move to

01:51:35.058 --> 01:51:39.178
adjourn. Is there a mover? Councelor Foxton. Councelor Huick.

01:51:39.274 --> 01:51:42.110
And you will be prompted in escribe to vote.

01:52:09.740 --> 01:52:13.440
Okay, that's carried off the chair.

01:52:14.540 --> 01:52:14.820
Thank.
